wifi: wcn36xx: validate scan bands against radio capabilities

WCN3620 registers only the 2.4 GHz band, but scan RX descriptors can
carry rf_band values that select the 5 GHz channel mapping. The receive
status then references an unsupported band and wcn36xx_update_survey()
dereferences a NULL supported-band pointer (sband->channels) from RX
interrupt context, producing "Fatal exception in interrupt".

Three guards, all no-ops on dual-band hardware:
  * only use the 5 GHz mapping when that band is actually registered;
  * reject frequencies absent from the registered channel tables before
    updating survey data or delivering the frame to mac80211;
  * bail out of survey update when the selected band is not registered.

Based on the upstream wireless postings (Alexander Vernel, 2026-10-13,
"validate scan bands against radio capabilities"; Zhaoyang Li, 2026-10-19,
"validate band and frequency in survey updates"), rebased onto the
backports-v7.2 txrx.c layout.

Link: https://github.com/msm8916-mainline/linux/commit/0be2d63a476e83c757d9caafc22eae00bcfd1df8
Fixes: 8a27ca394782 ("wcn36xx: Correct band/freq reporting on RX")
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c
@@ -286,6 +286,8 @@
 		idx = wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_2GHZ]->n_channels;
 
 	sband = wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[band];
+	if (!sband)
+		return;
 	channel = sband->channels;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < sband->n_channels; i++, channel++) {
@@ -367,7 +369,8 @@
 		 */
 		u8 hwch = (bd->reserved0 << 4) + bd->rx_ch;
 
-		if (bd->rf_band != 1 && hwch <= sizeof(ab_rx_ch_map) && hwch >= 1) {
+		if (wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ] &&
+		    bd->rf_band != 1 && hwch <= sizeof(ab_rx_ch_map) && hwch >= 1) {
 			status.band = NL80211_BAND_5GHZ;
 			status.freq = ieee80211_channel_to_frequency(ab_rx_ch_map[hwch - 1],
 								     status.band);
@@ -375,6 +378,9 @@
 			status.band = NL80211_BAND_2GHZ;
 			status.freq = ieee80211_channel_to_frequency(hwch, status.band);
 		}
+
+		if (!ieee80211_get_channel(wcn->hw->wiphy, status.freq))
+			goto drop;
 	} else {
 		status.band = WCN36XX_BAND(wcn);
 		status.freq = WCN36XX_CENTER_FREQ(wcn);
